{% comment %}
  App Embed: Wholesale (site-wide)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  This is an APP EMBED block (target: "body"), not a section block. It is enabled
  from the theme editor's "App embeds" panel with a single on/off toggle — no
  section placement required, so it can't be put in the wrong spot or forgotten
  on a template. This is the robust, site-wide host for the wholesale UI.

  What it does on every page, for logged-in wholesale customers:
    1. Emits <meta name="wh-customer" content="1"> so wholesale.js knows the
       customer is wholesale instantly — no async status call, no price flash.
    2. Loads wholesale.css + wholesale.js, which power the product-page
       wholesale price block and the account-dropdown Orders link rewrite.
       (Collection/search cards intentionally show no prices — matches the
       theme's cards, which are image + title only.)

  wholesale.js is idempotent (window.__whWholesaleInit guard), so loading it here
  AND from the product-page price block on a PDP is safe.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %} Shop-wide tag casing registry: writes of 'wholesale' can surface
   as legacy 'Wholesale', so the check must be case-insensitive. {% endcomment %}
{% assign wh_tag_str = customer.tags | join: '|' | downcase | prepend: '|' | append: '|' %}
{% if customer and wh_tag_str contains '|wholesale|' %}
  <meta name="wh-customer" content="1">
  {% comment %} Mark this browser as a wholesale account (localStorage, so it
     survives the storefront session cookie expiring) and reset the
     auto-relogin bookkeeping — see the anonymous branch below. {% endcomment %}
  <script>
    try {
      localStorage.setItem("wh_acct", "1");
      localStorage.removeItem("wh_relogin_at");
      localStorage.removeItem("wh_relogin_tries");
      sessionStorage.removeItem("wh_relogin");
    } catch (e) {}
  </script>
  {{ 'wholesale.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  <script src="{{ 'wholesale.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

  {% comment %}
    Wholesale top bar — a slim banner ABOVE the theme header with the two
    wholesale surfaces. The theme header (incl. cart) stays fully stock.
    Rendered hidden at the end of body; wholesale.js moves it to the top of
    <body> and reveals it (desktop only — on phones the wholesale UI doesn't
    activate at all and customers browse the retail site normally). If JS
    never runs, the bar simply stays hidden — graceful.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% liquid
    assign wh_ls_url = block.settings.linesheet_url | default: '/pages/linesheet'
    assign wh_orders_url = block.settings.orders_url | default: '/pages/orders'

    # Partner wording follows the account-type tag the app maintains
    # (wholesale accounts carry only 'wholesale'; distributor/b2b carry a
    # type tag alongside it). Topbar CSS renders this uppercase.
    assign wh_partner = 'a wholesale partner'
    if wh_tag_str contains '|distributor|'
      assign wh_partner = 'a distribution partner'
    elsif wh_tag_str contains '|b2b|'
      assign wh_partner = 'a CW&amp;T partner'
    endif
  %}
  <div class="wh-topbar" id="wh-topbar" hidden>
    <span class="wh-topbar-label">You are logged in as {{ wh_partner }}. Thank you for working with us. Questions? hello[at]cwandt.com</span>
    <nav class="wh-topbar-nav" aria-label="Wholesale">
      <a href="{{ wh_ls_url }}"{% if request.path == wh_ls_url %} class="wh-topbar-active" aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Order Sheet</a>
      <span class="wh-topbar-sep" aria-hidden="true">|</span>
      <a href="{{ wh_orders_url }}"{% if request.path == wh_orders_url %} class="wh-topbar-active" aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Order History</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
{% elsif customer %}
  {% comment %} Logged in but not (or no longer) wholesale: make sure the
     auto-relogin below never fires for this browser. {% endcomment %}
  <meta name="wh-customer" content="0">
  <script>try { localStorage.removeItem("wh_acct"); } catch (e) {}</script>
{% else %}
  <meta name="wh-customer" content="0">
  {% comment %}
    Auto-heal for the split-session state (bit Taylor and Frieda, 2026-07/08):
    the cwandt.com storefront session cookie expires independently of the
    long-lived account.cwandt.com portal session. The customer then looks
    logged in at the portal while the storefront treats them as anonymous, so
    the wholesale UI silently vanishes and the system "looks broken".

    If this browser has held a wholesale login before (wh_acct flag set
    above), bounce once through the new-customer-accounts OIDC endpoint,
    which returns to this exact page. Portal session alive → completes
    silently in under a second, storefront cookie restored, wholesale UI
    back. Portal session dead → the normal email-code login page, which is
    honest. Verified live on this store 2026-08-03 (return_to honored).

    Guards: once per tab (sessionStorage survives the round trip), at most
    once per 30 minutes per browser, and after 3 attempts that never landed
    back in the wholesale branch (which clears the counters) the flag is
    dropped entirely — an intentionally logged-out customer sees the login
    page a bounded number of times, never a loop.
  {% endcomment %}
  <script>
    (function () {
      try {
        if (localStorage.getItem("wh_acct") !== "1") return;
        var tries = Number(localStorage.getItem("wh_relogin_tries") || 0);
        if (tries >= 3) { localStorage.removeItem("wh_acct"); return; }
        if (sessionStorage.getItem("wh_relogin") === "1") return;
        var last = Number(localStorage.getItem("wh_relogin_at") || 0);
        if (Date.now() - last < 30 * 60 * 1000) return;
        sessionStorage.setItem("wh_relogin", "1");
        localStorage.setItem("wh_relogin_at", String(Date.now()));
        localStorage.setItem("wh_relogin_tries", String(tries + 1));
        location.replace(
          "/customer_authentication/login?return_to=" +
            encodeURIComponent(location.pathname + location.search)
        );
      } catch (e) {}
    })();
  </script>
{% endif %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Wholesale (site-wide)",
  "target": "body",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "linesheet_url",
      "label": "Linesheet page URL",
      "info": "Header 'Order Sheet' link. Defaults to /pages/linesheet."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "orders_url",
      "label": "Order history page URL",
      "info": "Header 'Order History' link. Defaults to /pages/orders."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
